#: who-iris/scripts/gen-iris-pages.ts:850
#. Continues the note above. Keep everything in <code> as written: they are field and command names.
msgid "The download links above point at where the bytes <em>are</em>, so they work. The claim in the catalogue is what is wrong, and <code>check:catalogue</code> does not check <code>localPath</code> at all — it verifies <code>metadataRef</code> and <code>libraryId</code>, and reports a clean run over three <code>materialized</code> claims that resolve to nothing."
msgstr ""

#: who-iris/scripts/gen-iris-pages.ts:803
#. Shown on every translated page. {language} is the language's own name. It states where the translation stops: the records are WHO's data and are never machine-translated.
msgid "The interface is shown in {language}. Publication titles, authors, abstracts and other catalogue records are shown as WHO published them."
msgstr ""

#: who-iris/scripts/gen-iris-pages.ts:881
#. The hero paragraph on the home page, as IRIS's own home page states it. Use the Organization's official names for its offices and Governing Bodies in your language.
msgid "The primary objective of the Institutional Repository for Information Sharing (IRIS) is to provide free digital access to the scientific and technical publications of the World Health Organization (WHO), including contributions from its Country Offices, Regional Offices, and Headquarters. Additionally, IRIS encompasses the mandates established by the Organization’s Governing Bodies in collaboration with its Member States."
msgstr ""

#: who-iris/scripts/gen-iris-pages.ts:827
